---
import Layout from "../layouts/Layout.astro"
import "../styles/global.css"

/**
 * Reserved for phase 2 — see PLAN.md.
 *
 * The route and the protocol role exist now so the split can happen without a
 * rewrite: the relay already accepts `role: "controller"` and gives it the same
 * privileged command surface and unredacted state as the host desk. What's left
 * is the UI, and the decision about which half of the controls lives where.
 */
---

<Layout title="NOGGIN’ — controller (planned)">
  <main class="mx-auto flex min-h-dvh max-w-lg flex-col justify-center gap-6 px-6 py-16">
    <div>
      <div class="font-display brass text-4xl">Controller</div>
      <div class="label mt-2" style="letter-spacing:0.3em">planned · phase 2</div>
    </div>

    <div class="rule-gold"></div>

    <p class="text-[13px] leading-relaxed text-muted">
      A second privileged screen, so the host can hold a tablet with the clue and
      the two buttons that matter while someone off to the side drives the rest of
      the board.
    </p>

    <ul class="space-y-2 text-[13px] text-muted">
      <li><span class="text-gold">Host tab</span> — clue, answer, correct/wrong, next. Nothing else.</li>
      <li><span class="text-gold">Controller</span> — grid, buzzer, scores, lifelines, timers, media cueing.</li>
      <li><span class="text-gold">Pairing</span> — same room code, scanned from the host desk.</li>
    </ul>

    <p class="text-[12px] text-faint">
      The relay already speaks to this role; only the interface is outstanding.
      Full notes in <code class="text-muted">PLAN.md</code>.
    </p>

    <a class="btn btn-gold self-start" href="/host">← Host desk</a>
  </main>
</Layout>
